(7501004, 1195238, 28742, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Art Roflmao:</b></div><hr/><i> "And when I came to, the wolf was standing over me with my arm in its'' mouth." </i></td></tr></table> <br/>You realize that was a quote from the 69th line of the lyrics from the famous Pink Floyd song "Peeling Paint, Covered With Ice, Seen Through A Magnifying Glass, Which Is Reflecting A Pine Tree"? Mind blown, huh?</td>', 'Originally posted by Art Roflmao: "And when I came to, the wolf was standing over me with my arm in its'' mouth."  You realize that was a quote from the 69th line of the lyrics from the famous Pink Floyd song "Peeling Paint, Covered With Ice, Seen Through A Magnifying Glass, Which Is Reflecting A Pine Tree"? Mind blown, huh?', '2017-02-20 02:00:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7501010, 1195176, 185719, '<td valign="top">dear people of DPC<br/> <br/>thank you all for your earnest votes and comments.. for those who voted well for me, i thank you all for likingg myy work.. it helps me to do what i love doingg.. and for those who voted me down, you guyys are the reason whyy i come here to improve on myy photographyy works..<br/> <br/>i have read through all of your comments, and sadlyy, no one guessed it correctlyy.. there is a scientific term for this part of the flower that produces pollen grains, which is the little lives i am talkingg about..<br/> <br/>and for the benefit of the doubt, the correct answer is: Stigma..<br/> <br/>nevertheless, thanks to you guyys for attemptingg to answer the question as to what is the thingg i am photographingg.. i appreciate your efforts!<br/> <br/>i hope i can continue to keep up the effort and produce myy best shots to you guyys, and most importantlyy, myself..<br/> <br/>thank you!<br/> <br/>regards<br/>zhihua</td>', 'dear people of DPC thank you all for your earnest votes and comments.. for those who voted well for me, i thank you all for likingg myy work.. it helps me to do what i love doingg.. and for those who voted me down, you guyys are the reason whyy i come here to improve on myy photographyy works.. i have read through all of your comments, and sadlyy, no one guessed it correctlyy.. there is a scientific term for this part of the flower that produces pollen grains, which is the little lives i am talkingg about.. and for the benefit of the doubt, the correct answer is: Stigma.. nevertheless, thanks to you guyys for attemptingg to answer the question as to what is the thingg i am photographingg.. i appreciate your efforts! i hope i can continue to keep up the effort and produce myy best shots to you guyys, and most importantlyy, myself.. thank you! regardszhihua', '2017-02-20 02:15:17.000000', NULL, 0),
